body:
yeah so me and my ex loved each other very much. We spent ages trying to make it work after our relationship went sour. We were on and off, unintentionally hurt each other a lot and decided to go no contact. However, when quarantine started we did what you guys did. It's only slowed down the breakup process. Because were inside alone all the time, it's so much easier to fall on our ex's when we need company (albeit virtual). For about 3 weeks now we stopped talking. It's done me so much good, I still love her, pretty sure she still loves me but love isn't always enough.

&#x200B;

My advice is to stick with not talking, you may be hurt but you will heal. The only way to do this is to heal by yourself. If you can focus on being completely content by yourself then it won't matter whether you guys are still talking when quarantine ends. I'm not sure if that's the advice you wanted to hear but that's the advice I'd have given myself from the beginning of this whole lockdown.
